# The lab tier installs neither the ProtonVPN tooling nor redshift, so their
# bar modules would shell out to binaries the target does not have.
#
# Applied to the DEPLOYED tree, which comes from this repo's home/ — not from
# a live $HOME. In that tree only ' ss protonvpn' is present: capture.sh
# already strips ' ss redshift' while building home/. The redshift rule is
# kept as a safety net for the day that duplicate strip moves out of
# capture.sh, where it does not belong.
s/ ss protonvpn//g
s/ ss redshift//g
